From 7f7ec9ee03595c4edce61bd8078c4e3e933d6f42 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ivory <contact@ivory.cafe>
Date: Fri, 11 Sep 2026 21:32:49 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 31/32] manager: embed an MCP server driven over an adb stdio
 bridge

UI automation to drive the pipeline (select/configure/enable/export) is fragile.
Add an in-app MCP (JSON-RPC 2.0) server so a host MCP client can drive it over
adb with no UI: config write and export must run in the app process (they need
r0dump_FusionConfig and MANAGE_R0DUMP_EXPORT), so the server lives in a
foreground service (McpBridgeService) hosting an abstract LocalServerSocket
'r0dump_mcp'; the r0dump_mcp_bridge native binary relays a client's stdio to it
(launch with 'adb shell r0dump_mcp_bridge' -- exec-out does not forward stdin on
all adb builds). Tools: read_status, list_apps, set_config, enable, disable,
repair_export, reusing FusionPropertyRepository/PackageRepository/
ArtifactExportRepository so behaviour matches the UI. A per-app MCP toggle
(Advanced tab, SharedPreferences-backed) starts/stops the service. Verified on
device: initialize/tools.list/read_status/list_apps and a set_config(defaults,
all)+enable round-trip published mask 0x2800000002d for com.icbc.elife with no
UI.
